{% doc %}
  Wraps a native <select> in a custom, styled dropdown (the "select-only
  combobox" pattern), so the open list matches the theme instead of the
  browser's native picker.

  The native select stays in the DOM as the source of truth: picking an option
  sets its value and dispatches a bubbling `change` event from it, so any code
  that already listens for changes on the select keeps working unchanged.
  Without JavaScript the native select is shown and works as usual.

  The button copies the select's classes, so it looks exactly like the styled
  select did; any decorative chevron placed next to `select-menu` rotates while
  the list is open. Style the open list per context through
  `.your-context .select-menu__list` (font, color) and the
  `--select-menu-radius` custom property (defaults to square corners).

  Option groups (<optgroup>) are kept as labelled groups in the list. A
  `hidden` option (a placeholder) shows on the button only, never in the list.
  While the select is disabled, the list doesn't open.

  The script is assets/select-menu.js, loaded on every page by the layout:
  the cart drawer renders this snippet into any page after load, and a
  snippet's own javascript tag only loads on pages that render it at load.

  The open list is positioned with `position: fixed` against the nearest
  transformed ancestor (e.g. the sidecart drawer) or the viewport, so scrolling
  containers can't clip it. It opens upward when there isn't room below and
  closes on scroll or resize.

  @param {string} select - The full <select> markup to enhance

  @example
  {% capture frequency_select %}<select class="my-select">...</select>{% endcapture %}
  {% render 'select-menu', select: frequency_select %}
{% enddoc %}

<select-menu class="select-menu">{{ select }}</select-menu>

{% stylesheet %}
  .select-menu {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
  }

  .select-menu.is-open {
    z-index: 30;
  }

  .select-menu--enhanced > select {
    display: none;
  }

  .select-menu__button {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .select-menu__list {
    position: fixed; /* placed by JS; escapes scrolling containers */
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 30;
    min-width: 160px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 6px 0;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: var(--select-menu-radius, 0);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(62, 32, 39, 0.12);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .select-menu__list[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .select-menu__group-label {
    padding: 8px 14px 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .select-menu__option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .select-menu__option.is-active {
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 7%, transparent);
  }

  .select-menu__check {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .select-menu__option[aria-selected='true'] .select-menu__check {
    visibility: visible;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
